# Terraform static site template

This repository contains a generalized Terraform template for deploying a static website using AWS and Cloudflare.

## Goals

- keep the site behind Cloudflare Zero Trust while it is private
- serve static content from S3 using EC2 instances
- route traffic to the domain through a Cloudflare tunnel
- keep deployment reproducible and easy to review
- avoid hardcoded sensitive identifiers in the repository

## Core infrastructure

- AWS VPC and private networking
- Amazon Linux 2023 EC2 fleet behind autoscaling
- NGINX serving content from S3
- Cloudflare tunnel for ingress
- Cloudflare Access gated preview
- DNS and TLS hardening

## Required inputs

See `terraform.tfvars.example` for the required values.

## Example deployment

```bash
cp terraform.tfvars.example terraform.tfvars
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

## Make public

To make the site public instead of private, remove or comment out the contents of `access.tf` before running `terraform apply`.

## Configuration notes

- `aws_profile` is optional if you are using default AWS credentials.
- `project_name` should be lowercase and hyphenated.
- `domain_name` should be a valid public domain or subdomain managed in Cloudflare.
